Good news: your DataTables setup is 90% correct 👍
The problem is NOT the table, NOT the markup, and NOT the DataTables library itself.

The issue is SCRIPT EXECUTION ORDER.


---

🚨 ROOT CAUSE (THIS IS THE REAL PROBLEM)

❌ Your DataTable initialization runs BEFORE jQuery & DataTables JS are loaded

In Create.cshtml, you have this:

<script>
    $(document).ready(function () {
        $('#itemsTable').DataTable({
            pageLength: 5,
            ordering: true,
            searching: true,
            lengthChange: false
        });
    });
</script>

But…

👉 This script is rendered inside @RenderBody()
👉 jQuery & DataTables are loaded AFTER @RenderBody() in _Layout.cshtml

So at runtime:

❌ $ is undefined
❌ DataTable() is not available yet
❌ Script silently fails

That’s why:

No search

No pagination

No error popup



---

✅ CORRECT FIX (DO THIS EXACTLY)

🔧 MOVE DataTable init INTO @section Scripts

❌ REMOVE this from Create.cshtml:

<script>
    $(document).ready(function () {
        $('#itemsTable').DataTable({
            pageLength: 5,
            ordering: true,
            searching: true,
            lengthChange: false
        });
    });
</script>


---

✅ ADD THIS instead (AT BOTTOM of Create.cshtml):

@section Scripts {

    <partial name="_ValidationScriptsPartial" />

    <script>
        $(document).ready(function () {
            if ($('#itemsTable').length) {
                $('#itemsTable').DataTable({
                    pageLength: 5,
                    ordering: true,
                    searching: true,
                    lengthChange: false
                });
            }
        });
    </script>

}

✔ This guarantees:

jQuery is loaded

DataTables is loaded

Table exists in DOM



